Package: gtmeta
Type: Package
Title: Information-Geometric Tools for Meta-Analysis
Version: 0.1.1
Authors@R:
    person("Willem M.", "Otte", email = "w.m.otte@umcutrecht.nl",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-1511-6834"))
Description: Implements information-geometric meta-integration (IGMI) for
    pooling study-level Gaussian evidence by Bures-Wasserstein,
    Fisher-Rao, and Wasserstein-Fisher-Rao geometry. The package provides
    constructors for univariate, multivariate, diagnostic-accuracy, and
    prediction-model study objects; Bures-Wasserstein barycenters;
    Fisher-Rao distances and Karcher checks; Frechet-variance
    heterogeneity measures; exact and bootstrap inference tools;
    robust Wasserstein-Fisher-Rao pooling; classical fixed-effect (FE),
    random-effects (RE), and unrestricted weighted least squares (UWLS)
    benchmarks; simulation generators; and Cochrane-style data adapters.
    Methods are described in Agueh and Carlier (2011)
    <doi:10.1137/100805741>, Chizat, Peyre, Schmitzer, and Vialard (2018)
    <doi:10.1007/s10208-016-9331-y>, DerSimonian and Laird (1986)
    <doi:10.1016/0197-2456(86)90046-2>, and Stanley and Doucouliagos
    (2015) <doi:10.1002/sim.6481>.
